    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4973\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to authorizing Cong Chasidei Bobov\nof Monsey to file an application for a real property tax exemption\n\nPURPOSE:  To authorize Congregation Chasidei Bobov of Monsey to file\nan application for a real property tax exemption.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the assessor of the town of Ramapo, Rockland\nCounty, to accept an application for exemption from real property\ntaxes pursuant to section 420-a of the Real Property Tax Law for the\n2011 assessment roll from Congregation Chasidei Bobov of Monsey for a\nparcel located at 80 Grove Street, Monsey, town of Ramapo.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  This bill would allow for a retroactive real property\ntax exemption for a parcel owned by Congregation Chasidei Bobov of\nMonsey, as requested by the Town.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
